{"step_index":1182,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:36:33Z","input_tokens":2432,"cache_read_tokens":140123,"output_tokens":4501,"thinking":"`EncryptedLocalDB` in `teacher.html` utilizes a concise pattern: `listRecords` conditionally passes an abort signal to `_req` using a ternary operator. The `subAbort` function handles abort errors effectively, specifically returning if the error's name is 'AbortError'. This design appears clean and avoids unnecessary conditional logic.\n\n\nThe `refreshSubmissions()` function suppresses error display after a request is aborted, which might be undesirable. The user's request involves UI changes related to auto-quiz functionality and the submissions page. Carefully reviewing the user's specific wording, especially the potential typo \"availbe\", is crucial to ensure accurate implementation of the requested UI changes. The plan needs to address hiding the \"Clear Students\" button when auto-record is disabled, while showing the new notice string.\n\n\nExisting submissions in Firestore won't be deleted when auto-record is turned off, and will also not be shown. A note should be added to the plan to clarify this. There's a potential edge case where the `teacher.html` page initially sets `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz = false` before asynchronously reading the saved Firestore setting, which could be true.\n\n\nWhen `Auto Record Quiz` is toggled off, the UI should hide the \"Clear Students\" button, submission count badge, and description, displaying a notice instead, while also stopping and aborting any in-flight requests. Conversely, when toggled on, those elements should reappear, and the submission poller should start if the submissions tab is active. The tab-switching logic needs to ensure the poller starts and stops at the correct times. There is a potential need to prevent a race condition involving the auto-record setting's initialization.\n\n\nThe submission poller needs to be immediately cleared and requests aborted upon tab minimization or backgrounding, using `clearInterval` and `subAbort.abort()`. A visibility change listener should be added to ensure the poller cleanly pauses and resumes. Additionally, it's crucial to examine the quiz download settings and template within Firestore, since changes to `index.html` necessitate compiling and hardening both `index.html` and `teacher.html`.\n\n\nThe plan now includes syncing the compiled quiz template to Firestore, ensuring the `autoRecordQuiz` gate applies to offline downloads. A patch entry will be added to the history.md file. Considering the `index.html` file, a check for potential edge cases concerning `isAutoRecord` with missing or undefined settings is underway, with the existing default behavior of defaulting to `true` preserved for backward compatibility.\n\n\nThe `teacher.html` code consistently saves `settings.autoRecordQuiz` as a boolean value, either `true` or `false`. This is confirmed through initialization, merging settings, serialization, and direct inspection of Firestore data. Consequently, the `isAutoRecord()` function in `index.html` reliably receives a boolean value for `autoRecordQuiz` from the settings. Now crafting the `implementation_plan.md` artifact.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to gate remote quiz submissions on autoRecordQuiz in index.html, display the auto-record-only notice while hiding Clear Students and halting polling in teacher.html when autoRecordQuiz is OFF, re-harden and sync the template, and verify all affected flows and callers.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan — Gate Submissions by Auto Record Quiz & Add Submissions Notice (`Patch 1.0.23`)\n\n## Investigation Summary & Root Cause\n1. **Unconditional remote submission write in `index.html` (`finish()`):**\n   - In `tmp_backup/index.html`, `const isAuto = st.autoRecordQuiz !== false;` is evaluated only when updating `#res-actions` / `#res-note`, **after** `EncryptedLocalDB.appendRecord(quizId, subData)` already ran unconditionally.\n   - Because of this, finishing a quiz on a quiz configured with `autoRecordQuiz: false` (`quizzes/active` currently has `autoRecordQuiz: { booleanValue: false }`) still downloaded `result_*.json` for the student **and** posted a submission document (observed in live Firestore: `1` submission `asd/asd`) to `quizzes/active/submissions`.\n2. **Unconditional submission polling & display in `teacher.html` (`#view-sub`):**\n   - `refreshSubmissions()` runs on boot, on tab switch, and every `4000ms` regardless of `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`, showing stale or inadvertently recorded submissions and displaying the `Clear Students` button (`#clear-sub-btn`) even when Auto Record Quiz is OFF.\n\n## Research & Optimization Rationale\n- **Gated Rest Write & Zero Allocation on Disabled Mode (`index.html`):** Checking `isAutoRecord()` **before** assembling `subData` skips payload object creation, `toStoreFields` Firestore serialization, and the outbound HTTP `POST` altogether when `autoRecordQuiz === false`.\n- **Single-Source Flag Helper (DRY):** Extracting `isAutoRecord()` removes duplicated inline checks (`st.autoRecordQuiz !== false`) shared between `finish()` and `showLock()`.\n- **Event-Driven Polling + Cancellation (`teacher.html`):** Following `AbortController` + Visibility API patterns for Firestore REST polling, `syncSubPoller()` runs `setInterval(..., 4000)` only when `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz && !document.hidden && !$('view-sub').classList.contains('hide')`, immediately clears the interval and aborts any in-flight `listRecords()` request when switching tabs, hiding the browser tab, or toggling Auto Record Quiz OFF—eliminating background reads and DOM thrashing.\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### 1. Pre-hardened Source: `scratch/obf_tool/tmp_backup/index.html` -> Compiled `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit\\index.html`\n- **Add shared helper `isAutoRecord()`:**\n  ```javascript\n  function isAutoRecord() {\n    return !quizData || !quizData.settings || quizData.settings.autoRecordQuiz !== false;\n  }\n  ```\n- **Update `finish()`:**\n  - Evaluate `const autoRec = isAutoRecord();` prior to constructing `subData`.\n  - Wrap `subData` construction and `EncryptedLocalDB.appendRecord(quizId, subData)` inside `if (autoRec) { ... }`.\n  - Reuse `autoRec` for toggling `$('res-actions').style.display` and `$('res-note').textContent`.\n- **Update `showLock()`:**\n  - Replace the duplicate inline settings check with `const isAuto = isAutoRecord();`.\n- **Zero UI/Behavior Leakage:** Local device lock (`localStorage.setItem(LOCK, ...)`), `ds_exam_results` history, Download/Copy result fallback, and silent mask/watermark behavior remain intact.\n\n### 2. Pre-hardened Source: `scratch/obf_tool/tmp_backup/teacher.html` -> Compiled `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit\\teacher.html`\n- **HTML (`#view-sub`):**\n  - Add `id=\"sub-desc\"` to the subtitle `<p>` inside `#view-sub` so it can be toggled cleanly alongside controls when Auto Record Quiz is OFF.\n- **CSS / Visibility Controls (`hide` class):**\n  - Reuse existing `.hide { display: none !important }` to remove `#clear-sub-btn`, `#sub-count-badge`, and `#sub-desc` from both layout and keyboard/accessibility focus when `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`.\n- **JS Submission Notice, Polling & Modal Guard:**\n  - Update `EncryptedLocalDB.listRecords(id, signal)` to forward `{ signal }` into `_req(url, ...)` when provided.\n  - Add `syncSubViewState()` & `stopSubPoller()` / `syncSubPoller()`:\n    - When `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`:\n      - Stop any active submission polling timer (`clearInterval(subPollId)`) and abort any in-flight `listRecords` request (`subAbort`).\n      - Add `.hide` to `#clear-sub-btn`, `#sub-count-badge`, and `#sub-desc`.\n      - Display `<p style=\"text-align:center;padding:24px;color:var(--mu);margin:0\">Notice: This is only available to auto record quiz</p>` in `#sub-feed`.\n    - When `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` is `true`:\n      - Remove `.hide` from `#clear-sub-btn`, `#sub-count-badge`, and `#sub-desc`.\n      - Only fetch/poll submissions when `#view-sub` is active (`!$view.classList.contains('hide')`) and `!document.hidden`, avoiding wasted boot fetches before `loadTeacherQuiz()` resolves or background polling when viewing Quiz Editor / Reset.\n  - Wire `syncSubViewState()` into `syncOptionsUI()` (covers both `loadTeacherQuiz()` / `populateQuizData()` hydration and manual `#btn-auto-rec` toggles), and wire `syncSubPoller()` into `switchTab()` and a single `document.visibilitychange` listener.\n  - Guard `refreshSubmissions()` at entry: if `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`, call `syncSubViewState()` and return immediately without network I/O; ignore `AbortError` cleanly on cancelled polls.\n  - Guard `modal-yes-btn` (`action === 'clearSub'`) against `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` in case state toggled while the modal was open.\n\n### 3. Hardening, Template Sync & Documentation\n- Re-harden both `index.html` and `teacher.html` using `scratch/obf_tool/harden.cjs` (dual-layer AST obfuscation + RC4 stream cipher, verifying 0 in-code comments, 0 forbidden plaintext strings, and `< 900KB` output ceiling).\n- Sync compiled `index.html` to Firestore `quizzes/template` (`updateMask.fieldPaths=html&updateMask.fieldPaths=updatedAt`) so `Download Quiz File` embeds the updated remote-submission gate.\n- Append Non-Major `Patch 1.0.23` entry below `Patch 1.0.22` in `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit\\HISTORY.md` (with why).\n- **Untouched files:** `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` (never touched), existing remote submission data in `quizzes/active/submissions` (left untouched unless you explicitly ask to clear it).\n\n## Dependency & Affected Flow Inventory\n- **`index.html`:** `finish()` (manual result mode vs auto-record mode), `showLock()` (`#lkdl` button visibility on locked reload), `loadQuiz()` (local/vault settings hydration via `quizData.settings.autoRecordQuiz`), `dlRec()` / `#cp` (Download Result File & Base64 Copy fallback).\n- **`teacher.html`:** `loadTeacherQuiz()` -> `populateQuizData()` -> `syncOptionsUI()`, `#btn-auto-rec` click toggle, `switchTab()` (`Quiz Editor` / `Submissions` / `Reset`), `refreshSubmissions()`, `clear-sub-btn` -> `#confirm-modal` -> `purgeRecords()`, `#dl-quiz-btn` (`Download Quiz File` template embedding via `quizzes/template`).\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Unsaved toggle mismatch:** Flipping `Auto Record Quiz` ON in `teacher.html` reveals the Submissions tab UI locally, while live student links continue using whatever setting was last saved to Firestore until `Save to Quiz` is clicked (consistent with every toggle in Options). No automatic save on toggle will be added unless requested.\n- **Spelling note:** Adjusting `\"availbe\"` to `\"available\"` (`\"Notice: This is only available to auto record quiz\"`). Please confirm if you want the exact original typo instead.\n\n## Verification Plan (Post-Final Edit)\n1. **Pre- & Post-Hardening Static Audits:** Verify syntax, 0 comments (`//`, `/*`, `<!--`), 0 forbidden traces (`firebase`, `firestore`, `fetch`, etc.), byte sizes `< 900KB`, and unchanged `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`.\n2. **Gate Verification in `index.html` (Node VM Mock):**\n   - With `autoRecordQuiz: false`: finish quiz -> verify `0` `POST` calls made to `submissions`, `#res-actions` visible (`display: flex`), `#res-note` shows manual instructions, `localStorage` lock saved, and `showLock()` reload shows `#lkdl`.\n   - With `autoRecordQuiz: true` and legacy `settings: undefined`: finish quiz -> verify `1` `POST` submission sent, `#res-actions` hidden (`display: none`), `#res-note` shows auto-submitted text, and `showLock()` reload keeps `#lkdl` hidden.\n   - Verify offline `#local-db-vault` fallback with sealed `autoRecordQuiz: false` payload also suppresses remote submission.\n3. **Submissions View & Notice Verification in `teacher.html` (Node VM Mock):**\n   - Load quiz with `autoRecordQuiz: false`: verify `#clear-sub-btn.classList.contains('hide') === true`, `#sub-count-badge.classList.contains('hide') === true`, `#sub-desc.classList.contains('hide') === true`, `#sub-feed` displays `Notice: This is only available to auto record quiz`, and switching to `#tab-btn-sub` triggers `0` `listRecords` network requests even when stale remote submissions exist.\n   - Toggle `#btn-auto-rec` ON -> switch to `#tab-btn-sub`: verify `#clear-sub-btn` and `#sub-count-badge` unhide, submissions load/render properly, polling interval runs ONLY while `#view-sub` is active and `!document.hidden`, and switching back to `Quiz Editor` or `Reset` stops polling immediately.\n   - Toggle `#btn-auto-rec` back OFF -> verify `#clear-sub-btn` hides again, `#sub-feed` reverts to Notice, polling stops, and `Clear Students` action is blocked if `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`.\n4. **Regression Suites & Live Check:** Re-run `verify_hardened.cjs`, `verify_reset_tab.cjs`, and `verify_stealth_mask.cjs` after compilation and template sync; inspect `quizzes/template` sync HTTP 200. (Browser visual rendering & manual mobile interaction remain unverified in headless Node.)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
