{"step_index":1184,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:37:00Z","input_tokens":4611,"cache_read_tokens":142556,"output_tokens":1021,"content":"I found why submissions were still being recorded and have prepared the plan in [implementation_plan.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md).\n\n### Root Cause Found\n- In [`finish`](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/scratch/obf_tool/tmp_backup/index.html#L664-L751) inside [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html), `EncryptedLocalDB.appendRecord(quizId, subData)` runs unconditionally before `autoRecordQuiz !== false` is checked—so even though `quizzes/active` has `autoRecordQuiz: false` and showed your Download/Copy buttons ([result_asd_asd.json](file:///f:/Downloads/result_asd_asd.json)), it still uploaded `asd / asd` to Firestore `quizzes/active/submissions`.\n- In [teacher.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html), [`refreshSubmissions`](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/scratch/obf_tool/tmp_backup/teacher.html#L740-L764) and its `4000ms` interval run without checking `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`, keeping `Clear Students` (`#clear-sub-btn`) visible and polling submissions anyway.\n\n### Proposed Fix (`Patch 1.0.23`)\n1. **[index.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html):** Extract `isAutoRecord()` and gate `subData` creation + `EncryptedLocalDB.appendRecord(...)` behind it so nothing is sent remotely when `Auto Record Quiz` is `OFF`, then re-harden and sync to `quizzes/template`.\n2. **[teacher.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html):** When `!settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`, hide `#clear-sub-btn`, `#sub-count-badge`, and the subtitle via `.hide`, stop/abort submission polling immediately, and display:\n   `Notice: This is only available to auto record quiz` *(adjusted from `\"availbe\"` — let me know if you want the exact original typo instead)*.\n3. Keep the leftover `asd / asd` record in Firestore untouched unless you want me to delete it as well.\n\nPlease review [implementation_plan.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md) and confirm if you'd like me to proceed (and whether to clear that leftover `asd / asd` test entry).","thinking":"Initial review of the codebase focuses on `index.html`, `teacher.html`, a JSON result file, and Firestore data. Suspect potential inconsistencies may exist within these data points. Need to examine how these elements interact to understand the failure.\n\n\n"}
